lifeos-nix patch f-siri-retire — do not load the Siri voice-turn endpoint

PROBLEM
  Pulse loads modules/siri.ts unconditionally ("always load; fails closed without
  SIRI_API_KEY") and routes POST /api/siri/turn to it — a tunnel-exposed door that sat
  dormant. It drives claude through the Agent SDK, which runs the SDK's own bundled binary
  and so bypasses the lifeos-nix claude wrapper and its [inference] gate (code review
  2026-10-04): a local-only install could still reach Anthropic through it.

FIX
  Remove the dynamic import and the /api/siri route from pulse.ts (Klemen, 2026-10-04:
  retire it like iMessage). modules/siri.ts stays on disk, unreferenced.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One file (pulse.ts), two hunks; disjoint from f-derived-watch-wire (loadModules tail) and
  0029 (shutdown handler).

VERIFICATION
  `rg siriModule pulse.ts` → no match; pulse.ts transpiles (bun build --no-bundle).

